From: Utsav Agarwal <utsav.agarwal@analog.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Nov 2023 15:59:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sc5xx: Add developer mode boot-mode override in SPL

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded specific]

Lets a developer pick the SPL boot device at runtime by writing a boot
mode index to a fixed address (0x82000000) over JTAG, instead of
rebuilding for each boot mode. Touches arch/arm/mach-sc5xx/spl.c, which
is ADI SC5xx SoC support with no upstream counterpart, and the fixed
address is specific to this memory map.

Applied only when DEVELOPER_MODE is set, via the conditional SRC_URI
append in u-boot-adi.inc:59, so production builds do not carry it.

Provenance reconstructed 11-Sep-2026 while adding the missing
Upstream-Status header. The patch reached this layer with no git header
at all, added in lnxdsp-adi-meta commit 30b2d1f "Adding patch for
enabling developer options" (Utsav Agarwal, 2023-11-08); the author and
date above are taken from that commit. No upstream U-Boot commit id is
recorded because the change was never submitted.
---
 arch/arm/mach-sc5xx/spl.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sc5xx/spl.c b/arch/arm/mach-sc5xx/spl.c
index 68e0310f5af..362263bdb0c 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sc5xx/spl.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sc5xx/spl.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ static int adi_sf_default_cs = CONFIG_SF_DEFAULT_CS;
 static int adi_sf_default_speed = CONFIG_SF_DEFAULT_SPEED;
 
 u32 bmode;
+#define BMODE_ADDR 0x82000000
 
 int spl_start_uboot(void)
 {
@@ -45,6 +46,18 @@ unsigned int spl_spi_get_default_cs(void)
 void board_boot_order(u32 *spl_boot_list)
 {
 	const char *bmodestring = sc5xx_get_boot_mode(&bmode);
+	int i = 0;
+	static char *bmodes[] = {
+		"JTAG/BOOTROM",
+		"QSPI Master",
+		"QSPI Slave",
+		"UART",
+		"LP0 Slave",
+		"OSPI",
+#ifdef CONFIG_SC59X_64
+		"eMMC"
+#endif
+	};
 
 	printf("ADI Boot Mode: 0x%x (%s)\n", bmode, bmodestring);
 
@@ -54,6 +67,18 @@ void board_boot_order(u32 *spl_boot_list)
 	 */
 	spl_boot_list[0] = BOOT_DEVICE_BOOTROM;
 
+	bmode = *((unsigned int *) BMODE_ADDR) - 1;
+ 	printf("Entering Developer Mode...\n");
+ 	if ((ARRAY_SIZE(bmodes) <= bmode) || (0 >= bmode)) {
+ 		printf("Please enter a bootmode at 0x%08x via JTAG:\n",BMODE_ADDR);
+ 		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(bmodes); i++)
+ 			printf("[%d]	%s\n", i+1, bmodes[i]);
+ 		
+ 		bmode = 0; //allow continuing to load U-boot proper if needed
+ 	} else {
+ 		printf("Booting into %s\n", bmodes[bmode], bmode);
+ 	}
+
 	if (bmode == 0) {
 		printf("SPL execution has completed.  Please load U-Boot Proper via JTAG");
 		while (1)
